Fix libei pointer input on multi-monitor layouts (GNOME/KDE portal path).

1. wayland/mod.rs clamped every libei click/move/drag point to the size of
   ONE wl_output, so on a 3840+3840 layout x was pinned to 3839: clicks on
   the second monitor landed on the first monitor's right edge.
2. wayland/libei.rs subtracted the EIS region offset before
   motion_absolute. Per the ei protocol, libei and libeis, absolute
   coordinates are desktop-layout positions that must lie inside a
   region; the offset is the region's place in that layout. Mutter's
   logical-monitor viewport transform is the identity.

Points are now sent unchanged and refused when they lie outside every
announced region (EIS would drop the motion and the button would land
where the pointer already was).

Observed on GNOME 49 (Mutter 49.6), two 3840x2160 monitors side by side,
cua-driver 0.38.0.

Upstream: https://github.com/trycua/cua/issues/5808
Tracking: issues/cua-driver-libei-multimonitor.md

